# Line endings, enforced on checkout on every OS.
#
# Go and shell sources must be LF. A Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true otherwise hands gofmt CRLF, which it always flags —
# so a file can pass every local gate and still fail PR CI on Linux
# (PR #62's backend job died exactly this way). Rust is unaffected
# (cargo fmt normalizes) and stays under the default text handling.
*.go text eol=lf
# The Go tools always write go.mod and go.sum with LF. With core.autocrlf=true
# a CRLF checkout of these files showed as modified forever, with no content change.
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
